<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cankili II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1621">1621</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sankili II, Cankili Kumaran</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cankili II was the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jaffna">Jaffna</a>, in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a>, who seized power in 1617 as regent. He resisted the Portuguese with help from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thanjavur">Thanjavur</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nayaka">Nayaks</a> and Malabar privateers, but the Portuguese under Filipe de Oliveira conquered the kingdom in 1619. He was taken to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/goa">Goa</a> and executed in 1621.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cankili-ii.jpg" alt="Cankili II" width="320" height="469" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AntanO · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:King_Cankili_II%27s_statue.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
